  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe built-in **VMC 3-axis** (`assets/machines/vmc.mch`) and **Tilt-head 5-axis** (`assets/machines/tilthead.mch`) stated machine-frame strokes (Z `-500..0`, X `±300`, Y `±250`), but the limit checker (`app::machine::check_document`) reads travel bands in **program coordinates through the work offset**. Every move above the Z0 work origin was out of stroke, so no program posted on the built-in VMC.\n\nFix: restate both files the way the Tormach files already are (b189c960): a slide of stroke L is `-L..L`, the full stroke either way, because the file cannot know where the work offset sits along the slide. Now Z `-500..500`, X `-600..600`, Y `-500..500`. No checker code changed. The rule is written down in the `app::machine` module doc and `assets/machines/AGENTS.md`. Test-fixture comments in `tilt.rs`, `rotary_verify.rs` and `post_not_judged.rs` that cited the old `-500..0` band were updated (comments only). The decision is recorded in `docs/decisions/457-vmc-z-stroke.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New `crates/app/tests/vmc_stroke.rs`:\n  - `a_plate_contour_on_the_built_in_vmc_passes_the_stroke_and_posts`: the issue's repro (2D Contour on a 1 mm plate, clearance Z 26, built-in VMC as the document machine). `check_document` is clean, `verification_report` has no problems, and `post_setup` posts. On the old `vmc.mch` this fails with the reported `... reaches 1.000 in Z, the stroke is -500.000..0.000` flood.\n  - `a_clearance_past_the_vmc_column_still_refuses_by_name`: clearance Z 520 is refused with `2D Contour1: move N reaches 520.000 in Z, the stroke is -500.000..500.000`, and the post is refused.\n- These suites all passed (debug): `vmc_stroke`, `machine`, `machine_library`, `posting`, `tormach_post`, `tormach_machines`, `tilt`, `rotary_verify`, `post_not_judged`, `setup_sheet`, `inverted_post`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `lathe.mch` (X `0..320`, Z `-615..0`) and `millturn.mch` (X `0..650`, Z `-620..0`) are unchanged. They still state one-sided bands that may refuse approach moves in front of the face. They need their own decision.\n- I did not run the headless MCP repro (`camcraft-cli mcp`), the GUI, or the ui crate suites. The ui crate is untouched, and its tests reference the VMC by name only.\n- Posted G-code does not change for any machine. The script mirror carries no linear travel, so the golden NC files are unaffected.\n\nChangelog: The built-in VMC 3-axis and Tilt-head 5-axis machines state their strokes in program coordinates (full stroke each way), so ordinary programs post instead of being refused for every retract above Z0.\n\nFixes #457\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
